<div class="text-center py-5">
  <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_NAME", "MentorFire Demo") %></h1>
  <p class="lead text-muted mt-2"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_TAGLINE", "") %></p>
  <p class="text-muted mx-auto mt-3" style="max-width: 640px;">
    Most mentoring is coffee with no structure, and it fizzles by the third meeting because nobody said when it
    would end. Write down what you have actually done and who it is for. MentorFire drafts a Program from it, in
    your voice: exactly the number of sessions you choose, an agenda for each that fits the time, starter tasks for
    you or your mentee, and three questions for a first intro. It never invents a credential and never judges
    anyone.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 d-flex justify-content-center gap-3">
    <% if signed_in? %>
      <%= link_to "Go to my offers", mentor_offers_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to "Try it free", sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
      <%= link_to "Sign in", sign_in_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<hr class="my-5 opacity-25">

<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 860px;">
  <h2 class="h5 text-muted text-center mb-4">Example &mdash; a fictional market stallholder&rsquo;s offer</h2>

  <div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="text-muted small mb-1">What I have actually done</p>
      <p class="mb-0 fst-italic">
        &ldquo;I ran a weekend bread stall at the Saturday market for nine years. The first summer I priced by what
        felt fair and lost money every week until I counted what each loaf actually cost me. The worst day was the
        October morning the canopy blew over&hellip;&rdquo;
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted small mt-2 mb-0">4 sessions of 60 minutes</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3 class="h5 mb-2">A first season behind the stall</h3>
      <blockquote class="outcome small mb-0">
        By the last session, the mentee has priced their goods from what each one costs, traded a Saturday, and keeps
        a notebook that tells them what to bring next week.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ol class="session-timeline list-unstyled small mb-3">
    <li class="session-step"><strong>1. What each loaf really costs</strong> <span class="text-muted">&middot; 60 of 60 min</span></li>
    <li class="session-step"><strong>2. Setting up for the weather</strong> <span class="text-muted">&middot; 60 of 60 min</span></li>
    <li class="session-step"><strong>3. The first Saturday, read back</strong> <span class="text-muted">&middot; 60 of 60 min</span></li>
    <li class="session-step"><strong>4. Running it alone</strong> <span class="text-muted">&middot; 55 of 60 min</span></li>
  </ol>

  <ul class="list-unstyled small mb-0">
    <li class="mb-1"><span class="badge assignee-badge assignee-mentee me-1">mentee</span> Price every item on the list from its cost, time counted</li>
    <li class="mb-1"><span class="badge assignee-badge assignee-mentor me-1">mentor</span> Stop by the stall on the first Saturday for ten minutes, to watch rather than help</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="text-center text-muted small mt-4">
    AI-generated. A first draft for the mentor to edit, built only from their words. It never judges anyone.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="text-center mt-5 pb-4">
  <% unless signed_in? %>
    <%= link_to "Draft your own Program &rarr;".html_safe, sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="mt-3 text-muted small">
    Open source &middot;
    <a href="https://mentorfire.com" class="text-muted">MentorFire</a>
  </div>
</div>
